---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Chrome from '../components/Chrome.astro';
import SiteFoot from '../components/SiteFoot.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/+$/, '');
---

<Base title="About the studio" description="Studio No Frame is a research-based practice of spatial and visual experience in Berlin, working across spatial design, scenography and exhibition architecture. Led by Yelta Köm. Partners include HKW, Pera Museum, SALT, Museum Ludwig and the Venice and Istanbul biennials.">
  <Chrome here="about" />
  <section class="page">
    <h1>Exhibitions as research.</h1>

    <div class="body">
      <p>
        Studio No Frame is a research-based practice of spatial and visual
        experience, based in Berlin. It works across spatial design, scenography
        and exhibition architecture, with artists, cultural institutions,
        project spaces and universities.
      </p>
      <p>
        Its structure is flexible and its team is mixed by design. The practice
        values collective thinking, experimental methods and process-oriented
        making.
      </p>

      <h2>Partners</h2>
      <p>
        Haus der Kulturen der Welt, Istanbul Foundation for Culture and Arts
        (İKSV), Istanbul Modern, Museum Ludwig, MAXXI Rome, Pera Museum, SALT,
        La Biennale di Venezia, the Istanbul Biennial, the Istanbul Design
        Biennial and the Timișoara Biennial. Artists we have worked with
        include Abbas Zahedi, Ahmet Öğüt, Amy Lien &amp; Enzo Camacho, Ayşe
        Erkmen, Füsun Onur, Gülsün Karamustafa, Leman Darıcıoğlu, Monira Al
        Qadiri, Raul Walch and Tomás Saraceno.
      </p>

      <h2>Team</h2>
      <p>
        The studio is led by <strong>Yelta Köm</strong>, an Istanbul-born
        architect and artist who has lived and worked in Berlin for over a
        decade. His practice centres on spatial interventions and temporary
        setups built with institutions, artists and communities.
      </p>
      <p>
        We work with a rotating group of designers, researchers and production
        managers, and we bring in collaborators to suit each exhibition rather
        than fitting every show to a fixed team.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Current team</strong><br />
        Kubilay Ercelep
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Former team and collaborators</strong><br />
        Ece Aktuğ, Gökalp Alaca, Ali Haydar Ararut, Selin Doğaner, Bengü Erdem, Pelin Gezer, Nisa Gökgöz, İdil Gökgöz, Deniz İnal, Serap Kaçmaz, Utku Kan, Melisa Karataş, Yesol Kim, Emek Şayan, Elif Tan
      </p>

      <h2>Working with us</h2>
      <p>
        To see the full portfolio or discuss a project,
        {' '}<a href={`${base}/contact`}>get in touch</a>. If you are looking for an
        internship, the details are on the
        {' '}<a href={`${base}/internships`}>internships page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <SiteFoot />
</Base>
